---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Notes on the next decade"
  description="How Dinesh Pai thinks about businesses, supply and demand, patient capital, and where he sees opportunities in India over the next decade."
  maxWidth="max-w-5xl"
  showProgress={true}
>
  <div class="space-y-16 py-2 font-serif">

    <!-- TITLE & OVERVIEW -->
    <header class="space-y-4">
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 !mt-0 !mb-2 leading-tight">
        Notes on the next decade
      </h1>
      <p class="font-serif text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Before getting into specific sectors, I want to share how I look at businesses and why only some of them become good investment opportunities.
      </p>

      <!-- Prominent Section Index -->
      <nav aria-label="Thesis sections" class="mt-6 p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-md border border-stone-300/90 dark:border-stone-700 bg-white/60 dark:bg-stone-900/50 space-y-3">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-stone-200/90 dark:border-stone-800 pb-2 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">
          <span class="font-bold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">On This Page</span>
          <span class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">01 to 06</span>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-2.5 font-mono text-xs">
          <a href="#first-principles" class="group flex items-baseline gap-2.5 p-2.5 rounded border border-stone-200/80 dark:border-stone-800 bg-white/70 dark:bg-stone-900/60 hover:border-brand-light dark:hover:border-brand-dark transition-colors">
            <span class="font-bold text-brand-light dark:text-brand-dark">01</span>
            <span class="font-medium text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 group-hover:text-brand-light dark:group-hover:text-brand-dark">First Principles</span>
          </a>
          <a href="#income-slabs" class="group flex items-baseline gap-2.5 p-2.5 rounded border border-stone-200/80 dark:border-stone-800 bg-white/70 dark:bg-stone-900/60 hover:border-brand-light dark:hover:border-brand-dark transition-colors">
            <span class="font-bold text-brand-light dark:text-brand-dark">02</span>
            <span class="font-medium text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 group-hover:text-brand-light dark:group-hover:text-brand-dark">Household Incomes</span>
          </a>
          <a href="#tax-filings" class="group flex items-baseline gap-2.5 p-2.5 rounded border border-stone-200/80 dark:border-stone-800 bg-white/70 dark:bg-stone-900/60 hover:border-brand-light dark:hover:border-brand-dark transition-colors">
            <span class="font-bold text-brand-light dark:text-brand-dark">03</span>
            <span class="font-medium text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 group-hover:text-brand-light dark:group-hover:text-brand-dark">Tax Filings</span>
          </a>
          <a href="#what-gets-scarce" class="group flex items-baseline gap-2.5 p-2.5 rounded border border-stone-200/80 dark:border-stone-800 bg-white/70 dark:bg-stone-900/60 hover:border-brand-light dark:hover:border-brand-dark transition-colors">
            <span class="font-bold text-brand-light dark:text-brand-dark">04</span>
            <span class="font-medium text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 group-hover:text-brand-light dark:group-hover:text-brand-dark">Consumer Scarcity</span>
          </a>
          <a href="#import-dependence" class="group flex items-baseline gap-2.5 p-2.5 rounded border border-stone-200/80 dark:border-stone-800 bg-white/70 dark:bg-stone-900/60 hover:border-brand-light dark:hover:border-brand-dark transition-colors">
            <span class="font-bold text-brand-light dark:text-brand-dark">05</span>
            <span class="font-medium text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 group-hover:text-brand-light dark:group-hover:text-brand-dark">What India Imports Today</span>
          </a>
          <a href="#sovereign-infra" class="group flex items-baseline gap-2.5 p-2.5 rounded border border-stone-200/80 dark:border-stone-800 bg-white/70 dark:bg-stone-900/60 hover:border-brand-light dark:hover:border-brand-dark transition-colors">
            <span class="font-bold text-brand-light dark:text-brand-dark">06</span>
            <span class="font-medium text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 group-hover:text-brand-light dark:group-hover:text-brand-dark">Industrial &amp; Sovereign Tech</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <!-- 01 / FIRST PRINCIPLES -->
    <section id="first-principles" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6">
      <div class="section-rule">
        <h2 class="section-heading">01 / First Principles</h2>
        <span class="section-meta">Businesses &bull; Supply &amp; demand &bull; Capital</span>
      </div>

      <!-- Split: Core business logic + Time to add supply minichart -->
      <div class="split-grid">
        <div class="text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base space-y-4">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">
            Why does a business exist?
          </h3>
          <p>
            A business exists to solve a problem a customer will pay for, at a cost lower than what they pay. Fundraising, valuations, and brand campaigns come later.
          </p>
          <p>
            Whether it stays profitable comes down to supply and demand. If ten others can set up the same supply in six months, competition will eat your margins. You see this with thin software tools and consumer brands using the same contract manufacturers. Everyone ends up spending heavily on marketing just to stay visible.
          </p>
          <p>
            Good businesses sit where demand is growing, but new supply takes years to build. You rarely find these gaps in macro reports. You find them by going deep into a niche: how the product is made, why current options fall short, and what stops someone from copying it quickly.
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure class="minichart-card">
          <figcaption class="chart-title">Time to Bring New Supply Online</figcaption>
          <p class="chart-sub">Typical lead time before new capacity works at scale</p>
          <div class="bars" style="--max:8">
            <div class="bar-row">
              <span class="bar-name">D2C brand via contract mfg</span>
              <div class="track">
                <span class="fill" style="--v:0.5"></span>
                <b class="val" style="--v:0.5">~6 mos</b>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="bar-row">
              <span class="bar-name">Thin software / SaaS workflow</span>
              <div class="track">
                <span class="fill" style="--v:0.75"></span>
                <b class="val" style="--v:0.75">6-9 mos</b>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="bar-row">
              <span class="bar-name">Farm-to-table dairy &amp; cold chain</span>
              <div class="track">
                <span class="fill green" style="--v:3.5"></span>
                <b class="val" style="--v:3.5">3-4 yrs</b>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="bar-row">
              <span class="bar-name">Hospitals, recovery care &amp; hotels</span>
              <div class="track">
                <span class="fill green" style="--v:4.5"></span>
                <b class="val" style="--v:4.5">4-5 yrs</b>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="bar-row">
              <span class="bar-name">CNC machines, grid &amp; propulsion</span>
              <div class="track">
                <span class="fill green" style="--v:6.5"></span>
                <b class="val" style="--v:6.5">5-8 yrs</b>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="axis">
              <span style="--v:0">0 yr</span>
              <span style="--v:2">2 yrs</span>
              <span style="--v:4">4 yrs</span>
              <span style="--v:6">6 yrs</span>
              <span style="--v:8">8 yrs</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="chart-note">
            The easier it is to add supply, the faster excess returns get competed away into customer acquisition costs.
          </p>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <!-- Sticky Rail: What makes it an investment opportunity -->
      <div class="rail-grid pt-2">
        <div class="rail-head space-y-3">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">
            What makes it an investment?
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">
            A good business is not always a good venture investment. Many good businesses can grow comfortably from their own customer cash flows. Outside capital only makes sense when it unlocks something that would not happen otherwise.
          </p>
        </div>

        <ul class="squares text-sm sm:text-base text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 leading-relaxed">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">Paid for without marketing dollars:</strong> Customers buy because the product solves a real problem, not for discounts.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">Supply is the moat:</strong> Whether it is village milk collection, soil testing, or five-axis machining, the hard part sits in physical execution rather than ad spend.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">Upfront effort turns into operating leverage:</strong> Building a factory, hospital network, or hardware product is slow early on. Once capacity fills up, unit costs fall and cash flows compound.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">Inelastic pricing power:</strong> Buyers care more about reliability, purity, or uptime than saving 5% on price. That leaves room for healthy margins without price wars.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">Capital that matches duration:</strong> If an engineering or supply chain problem takes six to eight years to solve, you cannot build it with money that needs a quick markup in two years.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Summary Table: First-Principles Lens -->
      <figure class="data-card">
        <div class="card-header">
          <div>
            <h3 class="card-title">How I Look at a Business</h3>
            <p class="card-subtitle">Three questions before looking at financial projections</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Layer</th>
                <th>Question</th>
                <th>What I Look For</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">1. The Business</th>
                <td class="font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Why does it exist?</td>
                <td>A clear problem customers will pay for without discounts.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="row-accent">
                <th scope="row">2. The Niche</th>
                <td class="font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">How hard is supply?</td>
                <td>Growing demand where new supply takes years of work or trust to build.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">3. The Capital</th>
                <td class="font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Why raise money?</td>
                <td>Capital goes into capacity, R&amp;D, or distribution that creates real impact.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <!-- 02 / HOUSEHOLD INCOMES -->
    <section id="income-slabs" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6">
      <div class="section-rule">
        <h2 class="section-heading">02 / Household Incomes</h2>
        <span class="section-meta">PRICE ICE 360&deg; Survey &bull; 2020-21 vs. 2030-31E</span>
      </div>

      <div class="text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base space-y-4 max-w-3xl">
        <p>
          The biggest shift in India over the next decade is in household incomes.
        </p>
        <p>
          In 2020-21, two-thirds of India's 301 million households earned less than ₹5 lakh a year. By 2030-31, the bottom two brackets will shrink in absolute numbers. Around <strong class="text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">74 million households will move into the middle class (₹5 to ₹30 lakh)</strong>, and another <strong class="text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">24 million will cross ₹30 lakh</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 100-Household Dot Grid Comparison (Cambrian-style grid100) -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="data-card">
          <div class="el-label">2020-21 Household Split</div>
          <div class="wealth-body mt-3">
            <div class="grid100" aria-hidden="true">
              {Array.from({ length: 100 }).map((_, i) => (
                <i class={i < 4 ? 'rich' : i < 35 ? 'on' : ''} />
              ))}
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="stat-hero text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-100">35 in 100</span>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 mt-1">
                households earned above ₹5 lakh a year (102M of 301M total). Only 4 in 100 earned above ₹30 lakh.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="data-card border-brand-light/40 dark:border-brand-dark/40">
          <div class="el-label">2030-31E Household Split</div>
          <div class="wealth-body mt-3">
            <div class="grid100" aria-hidden="true">
              {Array.from({ length: 100 }).map((_, i) => (
                <i class={i < 11 ? 'rich' : i < 58 ? 'on' : ''} />
              ))}
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="stat-hero text-brand-light dark:text-brand-dark">58 in 100</span>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 mt-1">
                households projected above ₹5 lakh a year (200M of 358M total). 11 in 100 cross ₹30 lakh.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Table 1: Household Income Slabs -->
      <figure class="data-card">
        <div class="card-header">
          <div>
            <h3 class="card-title">Indian Household Income Slabs</h3>
            <p class="card-subtitle">Constant 2020-21 prices &bull; Source: PRICE ICE 360&deg; Survey</p>
          </div>
          <span class="card-badge">301M &rarr; 358M Households</span>
        </div>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Income Group</th>
                <th>Annual Income</th>
                <th>2020-21</th>
                <th>2030-31E</th>
                <th>Share (21 &rarr; 31E)</th>
                <th>10Y Change</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Destitute</th>
                <td class="mono">&lt; ₹1.25 Lakh</td>
                <td class="mono">45M</td>
                <td class="mono">20M</td>
                <td class="mono">14% &rarr; 5%</td>
                <td class="mono text-stone-500">-56%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Aspirers</th>
                <td class="mono">₹1.25L to ₹5 Lakh</td>
                <td class="mono">154M</td>
                <td class="mono">138M</td>
                <td class="mono">52% &rarr; 37%</td>
                <td class="mono text-stone-500">-10%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="row-accent">
                <th scope="row">Middle Class</th>
                <td class="mono">₹5L to ₹30 Lakh</td>
                <td class="mono font-semibold">91M</td>
                <td class="mono font-semibold">165M</td>
                <td class="mono font-semibold">31% &rarr; 47%</td>
                <td class="mono pos">+81%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="row-accent">
                <th scope="row">Rich / Affluent</th>
                <td class="mono">&gt; ₹30 Lakh</td>
                <td class="mono font-semibold">11M</td>
                <td class="mono font-semibold">35M</td>
                <td class="mono font-semibold">4% &rarr; 11%</td>
                <td class="mono pos">+218%</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
            <tfoot>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Total India</th>
                <td class="mono">All Households</td>
                <td class="mono">301M</td>
                <td class="mono">358M</td>
                <td class="mono">100% (1.42B &rarr; 1.53B)</td>
                <td class="mono">+19%</td>
              </tr>
            </tfoot>
          </table>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <!-- 03 / TAX FILINGS -->
    <section id="tax-filings" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6">
      <div class="section-rule">
        <h2 class="section-heading">03 / Tax Filings</h2>
        <span class="section-meta">CBDT &amp; e-Filing Portal &bull; FY21 vs. FY26</span>
      </div>

      <div class="split-grid">
        <div class="text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base space-y-4">
          <p>
            Survey projections can be off, so it helps to check them against actual income tax returns.
          </p>
          <p>
            Between FY21 and FY26, individual tax filings grew from <strong class="text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">6.37 crore to 8.22 crore</strong>, driven by higher brackets. Filings under ₹5 lakh dropped 20%, while the <strong class="text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">₹5 to ₹10 lakh bracket grew 81%</strong>. Filers between <strong class="text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">₹10 lakh and ₹50 lakh more than doubled to 1.50 crore</strong>, and those <strong class="text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">above ₹1 crore grew 128%</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            About 1.62 crore Indians now declare over ₹10 lakh a year, double the number from five years ago. Still, that is just over 1% of our population. The base is growing fast, and it is still early.
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure class="minichart-card">
          <figcaption class="chart-title">Tax Filers Above ₹10 Lakh</figcaption>
          <p class="chart-sub">Individual returns declaring gross income &gt; ₹10L</p>
          <div class="bars" style="--max:200">
            <div class="bar-row">
              <span class="bar-name">FY21 (77.8 Lakh filers)</span>
              <div class="track">
                <span class="fill" style="--v:77.8"></span>
                <b class="val" style="--v:77.8">77.8L</b>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="bar-row">
              <span class="bar-name">FY26 (1.62 Crore filers)</span>
              <div class="track">
                <span class="fill green" style="--v:162"></span>
                <b class="val" style="--v:162">1.62 Cr (+108%)</b>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="axis">
              <span style="--v:0">0</span>
              <span style="--v:50">50L</span>
              <span style="--v:100">1.0 Cr</span>
              <span style="--v:150">1.5 Cr</span>
              <span style="--v:200">2.0 Cr</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="chart-note">
            Includes ₹10L to ₹50L (1.50 Cr), ₹50L to ₹1 Cr (7.64L), and &gt;₹1 Cr (3.86L). Source: CBDT &amp; Income Tax Portal.
          </p>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <!-- Table 2: ITR Filings by Gross Total Income Slab -->
      <figure class="data-card">
        <div class="card-header">
          <div>
            <h3 class="card-title">Income Tax Filings by Slab</h3>
            <p class="card-subtitle">Individual ITRs filed &bull; Source: CBDT &amp; Income Tax Portal</p>
          </div>
          <span class="card-badge">6.37 Cr &rarr; 8.22 Cr Filers</span>
        </div>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Income Slab</th>
                <th>FY21 Filers</th>
                <th>FY26 Filers</th>
                <th>Share (FY26)</th>
                <th>5Y Change</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Up to ₹5 Lakh</th>
                <td class="mono">3.47 Cr</td>
                <td class="mono">2.76 Cr</td>
                <td class="mono">33.6%</td>
                <td class="mono text-stone-500">-20%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="row-accent">
                <th scope="row">₹5 Lakh to ₹10 Lakh</th>
                <td class="mono font-semibold">2.12 Cr</td>
                <td class="mono font-semibold">3.84 Cr</td>
                <td class="mono">46.7%</td>
                <td class="mono pos">+81%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="row-accent">
                <th scope="row">₹10 Lakh to ₹50 Lakh</th>
                <td class="mono font-semibold">72.2 Lakh</td>
                <td class="mono font-semibold">1.50 Cr</td>
                <td class="mono">18.3%</td>
                <td class="mono pos">+108%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="row-accent">
                <th scope="row">₹50 Lakh to ₹1 Crore</th>
                <td class="mono font-semibold">3.95 Lakh</td>
                <td class="mono font-semibold">7.64 Lakh</td>
                <td class="mono">0.93%</td>
                <td class="mono pos">+93%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="row-accent">
                <th scope="row">Above ₹1 Crore</th>
                <td class="mono font-semibold">1.69 Lakh</td>
                <td class="mono font-semibold">3.86 Lakh</td>
                <td class="mono">0.47%</td>
                <td class="mono pos">+128%</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
            <tfoot>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Total Returns</th>
                <td class="mono">6.37 Cr</td>
                <td class="mono">8.22 Cr</td>
                <td class="mono">100.0%</td>
                <td class="mono">+29%</td>
              </tr>
            </tfoot>
          </table>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <!-- 04 / CONSUMER SCARCITY -->
    <section id="what-gets-scarce" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6">
      <div class="section-rule">
        <h2 class="section-heading">04 / Consumer Scarcity</h2>
        <span class="section-meta">Rising incomes &bull; Tight physical supply</span>
      </div>

      <div class="split-grid">
        <div class="text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base space-y-4">
          <p>
            Once a family crosses ₹10 lakh in annual income, basic needs like grains, clothes, and mobile data are covered. Extra income goes toward a better home, travel, health, clean food, and savings.
          </p>
          <p>
            When millions of families want these things at once, physical supply struggles to keep up. You cannot build a good hotel, a clean dairy supply chain, or a hospital overnight. Japan in the 1970s, South Korea in the late 1980s, and China after 2008 went through this same shift after crossing $3,000 in per-capita GDP.
          </p>
          <p>
            India enters this phase with very low physical capacity per person, so the runway to build locally is long.
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure class="minichart-card">
          <figcaption class="chart-title">Hospital Beds per 1,000 People</figcaption>
          <p class="chart-sub">Inpatient &amp; recovery capacity across Asian economies</p>
          <div class="bars" style="--max:14">
            <div class="bar-row">
              <span class="bar-name">India (today)</span>
              <div class="track">
                <span class="fill green" style="--v:1.3"></span>
                <b class="val" style="--v:1.3">~1.3 beds</b>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="bar-row">
              <span class="bar-name">China</span>
              <div class="track">
                <span class="fill" style="--v:5.0"></span>
                <b class="val" style="--v:5.0">~5.0 beds</b>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="bar-row">
              <span class="bar-name">Japan &amp; South Korea</span>
              <div class="track">
                <span class="fill" style="--v:12.5"></span>
                <b class="val" style="--v:12.5">12+ beds</b>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="axis">
              <span style="--v:0">0</span>
              <span style="--v:3.5">3.5</span>
              <span style="--v:7">7.0</span>
